  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c68da49b-c9b1-5024-84d9-16ed7d171199" activityNameId="5dcb7a41-d12d-5501-a85c-29507fcf13ca" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Tallow, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Tallow, at plant
Refers to 1 kg of tallow at rendering plant. Since the process of meat and bone meal production is nearly the same as the production of tallow (all steps are common except the milling of the meal), a physical allocation of the processes has been applied. The inventory can therefore also be used as an approximation for meat and bone meal.;
Synonyms: animal fat, Talg; 
UUID: f6655fa7-785d-3dcf-8640-017969ab9db2
The inventory includes the transport from the slaughterhouse to the rendering plant and  further processing of slaughterhouse wastes to tallow. It includes  the energy demand for operating a rendering plant, in form of electricity and natural gas, the use of tap water, the output of wastewater and the building infrastructure. The animal husbandry and the process of slaughtering are not included, since the raw material is considered as waste. 
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Refers to a typical technology for tallow processing in Switzerland.
Time period: Based on data from the year 1999.
Production volume: 20'000 tons/year in Switzerland.
Sampling: Data come from one rendering plant in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f6655fa7-785d-3dcf-8640-017969ab9db2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
